# Environment variables examples/reference-app/cmd/server actually reads
# (configFromEnv in server.go, plus demo_users.go's own boot-time seed
# gate) -- every value below is read with os.Getenv, so this file is a
# reference for what to set, not something the app loads itself (there is
# no dotenv loader in this codebase; use your shell, a process manager, or
# `env $(cat .env.example | xargs) go run ./cmd/server` to apply it).
#
# Every variable here is OPTIONAL: configFromEnv falls back to a
# documented, zero-external-dependency development default for each one
# left unset, so `go run ./cmd/server` with none of this set genuinely
# boots a working standalone-mode server on SQLite. Copy this file to
# .env, fill in real values only for what you actually need to change, and
# never commit the real .env (see the repository's .gitignore).

# Deployment mode: "standalone" (default) or "distributed". See
# docs/internal/03-deployment-modes.md -- this is a topology choice, never
# an implementation choice (that is what APP_REDIS_ADDR below is for).
APP_DEPLOYMENT_MODE=standalone

# HTTP listen port. Defaults to 8080 when unset.
PORT=8080

# Path to the SQLite database file the standalone deployment mode opens.
# Defaults to reference-app.db (relative to the working directory) when
# unset.
APP_DB_PATH=reference-app.db

# Redis address ("host:port") for the EventBus seam. Leave unset (or
# empty) to keep the in-process bus the standalone preset resolves by
# default -- zero setup, nothing else needs to be running. Set this only
# to compose a real Redis-backed bus into the standalone deployment mode
# (docs/internal/03-deployment-modes.md's deployment-mode /
# implementation-composition orthogonality), e.g.:
# APP_REDIS_ADDR=localhost:6379

# OTLP/gRPC endpoint ("host:port") traces and metrics are pushed to.
# Leave unset (or empty) to keep go/observability's local exporters
# (stdout traces/metrics plus the /metrics scrape endpoint) -- the
# zero-setup default. Set it to push both signals to a collector, in
# either deployment mode (exporter choice is an implementation-composition
# question, never a mode one), e.g.:
# APP_OTLP_ENDPOINT=localhost:4317

# Six master/HMAC keys, each a hex-encoded 32-byte key (64 hex
# characters), protect config's Sensitive values, org's and notification's
# blind-indexed contact columns, pki's local signing-key storage, and
# authn's blind-indexed and PII-encrypted columns. Every one of them has a
# documented, recognizable, NON-SECRET development default the app falls
# back to when its variable is unset (server.go's devConfigKey and its
# siblings) -- convenient for local development, but never acceptable for
# a real deployment, since it is checked into this very repository's
# source.
#
# RECOMMENDED: set APP_ROOT_KEY alone. configFromEnv derives all six
# keys below from it via dbkit.DeriveKey (HKDF-SHA256, one distinct
# purpose string per key -- go/dbkit/AGENTS.md's "Key derivation" section
# has the mechanism and its honest trade-off). Generate one value with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
APP_ROOT_KEY=REPLACE_WITH_64_HEX_CHARS

# ADVANCED: any of the six variables below, set explicitly, always wins
# over what APP_ROOT_KEY would have derived for that same key -- set
# one only for fine-grained, independent rotation of that one key;
# APP_ROOT_KEY alone already covers every key left unset here.

# Master key the config module seals Sensitive configuration values with
# (config.WithCipher). The key that encrypts the configs table cannot live
# in that table, so it must come from the environment.
APP_CONFIG_KEY=

# HMAC key org's blind indexer normalizes and indexes invitation email
# addresses with (dbkit.NewBlindIndexer). Deliberately a SEPARATE secret
# from APP_CONFIG_KEY: an AES key must never double as an HMAC key
# (go/org/invitation.go's EmailSerializerName doc comment).
APP_ORG_INDEX_KEY=

# HMAC key the notification module's blind indexers normalize and index
# encrypted contact email/phone addresses with (dbkit.NewBlindIndexer).
# Deliberately a SEPARATE secret from APP_CONFIG_KEY, for the identical
# AES-key-must-never-double-as-an-HMAC-key reason APP_ORG_INDEX_KEY's
# comment gives. One key serves both the email and phone indexers -- their
# two normalizers keep the two index columns' inputs in disjoint canonical
# forms, so a shared key leaks nothing between them.
APP_NOTIFICATION_INDEX_KEY=

# AES key that seals go/pki's LocalSigner private-key column
# (pki.RegisterLocalKeySerializer) -- ultimately what authn's access
# tokens are signed with. Had NO override path before APP_ROOT_KEY
# existed; a deployment that set none of the keys on this page was running
# signing-key storage on a key committed to this repository's source.
APP_PKI_LOCAL_KEY_CIPHER_KEY=

# HMAC key authn indexes users.email_index/phone_index with
# (authn.WithBlindIndexKey), so a user can be found by email or phone
# without decrypting every row. Must stay IDENTICAL across restarts (and
# across an APP_ROOT_KEY rotation) or every already-stored index becomes
# unfindable. Had NO override path before APP_ROOT_KEY existed.
APP_AUTHN_BLIND_INDEX_KEY=

# AES key that seals authn's encrypted PII columns (email, phone, TOTP
# secrets) via authn.RegisterPIISerializer. Deliberately a SEPARATE secret
# from every other key on this page -- dbkit's key-separation rule applies
# across modules, not only within one. Had NO override path before
# APP_ROOT_KEY existed.
APP_AUTHN_PII_CIPHER_KEY=

# Gates the boot-time demo-user seed (demo_users.go). Unset -- the
# default -- means no demo accounts are registered at boot; the app still
# works, with demo_subject.go's X-Demo-User header remaining the only way
# to act as a demo user. Setting this to any passphrase registers three
# real demo accounts (demo-owner@example.com, demo-reader@example.com,
# demo-acme-only@example.com) on every boot, each with a real membership
# and a real rbac grant, so a browser visitor can sign in as any of them
# with this passphrase and no header involved. Not a value you need in
# production; it exists purely to gate a demo affordance behind a
# deliberate operator choice, never a hardcoded default. This variable
# seeds EXACTLY those three accounts: the demo platform-staff account
# (the rbac.SystemDomain platform administrator) has its OWN variable
# below and is never seeded from this one.
APP_DEMO_USERS_PASSWORD=

# Points the smile-simulation pipeline (cmd/server/smilesim.go) at an
# OpenAI-compatible images endpoint. Both unset -- the default -- is the
# zero-setup posture: no image-generation credential row is written at
# boot, and a simulate request dead-letters with the gateway's coded
# credential refusal until a provider is named. Set both together to
# write the platform-wide image credential at boot, exactly the pair
# cmd/server/server.go's buildServer reads straight off its config:
#
#   APP_AI_GATEWAY_IMAGE_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9000/v1
#   APP_AI_GATEWAY_IMAGE_API_KEY=<key the endpoint accepts>
#
# The API key here is NOT a secret by construction: it is the value a
# local or CI-only fake provider accepts -- the browser end-to-end suite
# boots its own throwaway provider and points this pair at it
# (examples/reference-app/web/playwright.config.ts), the same
# non-secret demo shape APP_DEMO_USERS_PASSWORD establishes. A real
# deployment's key travels the same variables and is this app's own
# documented operator wiring, never a committed value.
APP_AI_GATEWAY_IMAGE_BASE_URL=
APP_AI_GATEWAY_IMAGE_API_KEY=

# Gates the boot-time demo platform-staff seed (demo_admin.go's
# seedDemoPlatformStaff), INDEPENDENTLY of APP_DEMO_USERS_PASSWORD. Unset
# -- the default -- means no platform-staff account is registered at boot.
# Setting this to a passphrase registers
# demo-platform-staff@example.com on every boot: a real account whose only
# membership is rbac.SystemDomain, holding the built-in owner role there --
# every permission any module declared, go/admin's admin:* permissions
# included -- which is how an operator signs the admin console's demo
# account in. Its own variable is deliberate: the platform administrator
# must never be seeded from (and therefore share) the ordinary demo
# users' passphrase. Same non-secret gating role as APP_DEMO_USERS_PASSWORD.
APP_DEMO_PLATFORM_STAFF_PASSWORD=

# Failure-injection switch for the self-service clinic provisioning chain
# (cmd/server/self_service.go). TEST AND E2E RIGS ONLY -- never set it in
# a real deployment. Absent or 0 (the default) disables the injection and
# leaves every boot byte-identical to the variable never having existed.
# Set to a positive integer N, the server fails the first N provisioning
# attempts of EACH self-registered account -- the synchronous attempt
# inside the register request and the retry job's own attempts alike --
# and succeeds on every later attempt of that account. Every registration
# the process serves is affected while it is set, so drive it on a
# dedicated server instance and database.
#
# The browser e2e recovery gate uses N=1: a fresh self-service register
# fails its one synchronous provision, the first retry (short backoff)
# converges the clinic, and the gate signs in once after convergence --
# inside authn's per-account login budget, with no "retry until it
# passes" loop. Anything that is not a whole number, or a negative one,
# refuses boot naming this variable.
APP_FAIL_SELF_SERVICE_PROVISION=0

# Directory the server serves the app's built frontend from (frontend.go).
# Unset -- the default -- means the server serves no frontend at all: the
# composed API handler answers exactly as it did before the
# frontend-serving round, and the browser page comes from the vite dev
# server (`pnpm dev` in web/, which proxies /api to this server). Set it
# to a real build output (examples/reference-app/web/dist after `pnpm
# build`) to have the deployed product URL serve its own page: "/" and
# unknown non-API paths answer index.html with no tenant required,
# /assets/* serves the built files, and /api/* keeps its answers. The
# image round wires it for you: the Dockerfile builds the dist into the
# image at /app/web/dist and sets APP_WEB_DIST to it.
# APP_WEB_DIST=
